.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: ISC
.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt MBT_MSE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mbt_mse_client ,
.Nm mbt_mse_server ,
.Nm mbt_mse_selected ,
.Nm mbt_mse_incomplete
.Nd Message Stream Encryption over a connection
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In mbt/mse.h
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_mse_client "struct mbt_ev *ev" "struct mbt_conn *inner" "const uint8_t infohash[20]" "unsigned provide" "struct mbt_conn **out"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_mse_server "struct mbt_ev *ev" "struct mbt_conn *inner" "const void *seed" "size_t seedlen" "mbt_mse_skey_lookup lookup" "void *arg" "unsigned provide" "struct mbt_conn **out"
.Ft unsigned
.Fn mbt_mse_selected "struct mbt_conn *c"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_mse_incomplete "struct mbt_conn *c"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
MSE, also called Protocol Encryption, hides the BitTorrent handshake from
traffic shaping.
It uses a 768-bit Diffie-Hellman exchange and RC4.
It does not give real confidentiality.
.Pp
These functions wrap an
.Xr mbt_conn 3 .
The result is also a connection, so the peer layer needs no change.
.Fa provide
is a mask of
.Dv MBT_MSE_RC4
and
.Dv MBT_MSE_PLAINTEXT .
The second method hides only the handshake.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_mse_client
starts the handshake on an outgoing connection.
Data that the caller writes before the handshake ends is sent as the initial
payload.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_mse_server
starts the handshake on an accepted connection.
.Fa seed
holds bytes already read from
.Fa inner .
.Fa lookup
receives SHA1("req2" + infohash) and writes the infohash of the matching
torrent.
.Pp
The read callback does not fire until the handshake ends.
A failed handshake calls the event callback with a negative errno.
The handshake fails with
.Er ETIMEDOUT
after 20 seconds.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_mse_selected
returns the selected method, or 0 if the handshake is not done or
.Fa c
is not an MSE connection.
.Fn mbt_mse_incomplete
returns 1 for an MSE connection whose handshake did not finish.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn mbt_mse_client
and
.Fn mbt_mse_server
return 0 and take ownership of
.Fa inner ,
or return a negative errno and leave
.Fa inner
with the caller.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mbt_conn 3 ,
.Xr mbt_session 3
